<title>SPAIN: Repsol offer to employees 90 pct overbid.</title>
<headline>Repsol offer to employees 90 pct overbid.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spain's Repsol said on Tuesday an offer to employees to buy shares in its upcoming privatisation had been 90 percent oversubscribed, with demand for 8.5 million shares registered.</p>
<p>&quot;The total demand registered in the sale of shares destined for employees and retired workers has been 48.7 billion pesetas,&quot; the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The initial offer to employees of just over 4.5 million shares represents 1.5 percent of Repsol's stock, or 15 percent of that still held by the government.</p>
<p>Repsol said it would allot shares on a pro rata basis and would fix the share price for employees next Monday. The price cannot exceed the maximum of 6,327 pesetas fixed on Monday.</p>
<p>Spanish state holding company SEPI is selling its remaining 10 percent stake in Repsol this month.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom + 34 1 585 2161</p>
